One note on a translation detail worth being explicit about, since it is the kind of thing that could bite later: the Rust [38;5;10mdriver[0m calls libc [38;5;10mprintf[0m via [38;5;10mextern "C"[0m rather than [38;5;10mstd::io::stdout[0m. That is what makes byte-identical output achievable here, because both libraries share the process's single C [38;5;10mstdout[0m stream and its buffering behavior. Had the translation used Rust's own stdout, output would still be textually identical but interleaving and flush timing could differ from C when mixed with other C output.[0m[0m
